{"id": 10, "ts": 1780475435.1917787, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I agree with James that Candidate\u202fA\u2019s ability to anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, and his excellent spatial vision give him a solid foundation for the technical and decision\u2011quality demands of long\u2011distance flights.\u202fHowever, I wanted to bring Sarah\u2019s input on Candidate\u202fB into the comparison: B handles stress very well\u2014a clear advantage for the high\u2011pressure environment of international routes\u2014but has been described as grumpy and uncooperative, which raises serious concerns about crew cooperation and professional communication.\u202fThose teamwork issues directly counterbalance B\u2019s stress\u2011resilience strength, especially when we consider A\u2019s leadership qualities and overall reliability despite his unfriendly demeanor.\u202fGiven that crew cooperation is a non\u2011negotiable safety criterion, I remain provisional in favor of Candidate\u202fA, while noting that B\u2019s stress handling is a strength we should keep in mind if further evidence mitigates his teamwork concerns."}
