{"id": 32, "ts": 1780475596.227773, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I acknowledge James\u2019s clarification that we have no concrete evidence on Candidate\u202fA\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation, adaptability, or feedback orientation\u2014only the indirect hint that his strong leadership might help, while his \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d and \u201cnot open to new ideas\u201d labels raise concerns. Given that the panel\u2019s remaining gaps center on exactly these crew\u2011interaction and adaptability criteria for all candidates, I remain cautious about endorsing A as the final choice. While A\u2019s situational awareness, spatial vision, and leadership are compelling, the lack of positive evidence on his teamwork and openness to feedback means we cannot yet outweigh the comparable strengths of the other candidates, especially Candidate\u202fC\u2019s proven calmness, technical competence, and rapid decision\u2011making, which directly address core safety criteria. Therefore, I propose we shift our provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**, pending further discussion of his crew\u2011cooperation potential and willingness to develop."}
